  "rows": {
    "600.60.20(1)": {
      "explanation": "Section 600.60 defines its own building types. An apartment building has seven or more dwelling units. A detached houseplex has up to six dwelling units on one lot, is not attached to a neighbour, and has at least one unit above another. A fiveplex has five units and a sixplex has six, and each counts as a type of detached houseplex, not an apartment building. A house with a secondary suite is not a houseplex.",
